\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces  Different monotonic increase of the total fraction of students in the learned state over iteration number. The blue lines represent the PI mode while the orange lines represent the TI mode. Unless indicated, the parameters are fixed such that $N=64$, $\rho _0=0.5$, $\delta \lambda =0.2$ (fairly homogenous) and an Inner Corner SA for PI mode. (a)\nobreakspace  {}Plots for varied $\rho _0$-values, introducing varying degrees of shifts along the iteration (time) axis. (b)\nobreakspace  {}Plots for varied $\delta \lambda $-values. (c)\nobreakspace  {}Representative development of classroom spatial configuration ($L=32$, $\rho _0=0.3$) observed for different iteration numbers from $t=2$ (each column doubles the previous $t$) for TI (first row) and PI (second row) modes. The learned and unlearned states are differentiated by the color intensity, with $\lambda =0.9$ (darker) and $0.1$ (lighter) shades. }}{5}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:comparison rates}{{4}{5}{Different monotonic increase of the total fraction of students in the learned state over iteration number. The blue lines represent the PI mode while the orange lines represent the TI mode. Unless indicated, the parameters are fixed such that $N=64$, $\rho _0=0.5$, $\delta \lambda =0.2$ (fairly homogenous) and an Inner Corner SA for PI mode. (a)~Plots for varied $\rho _0$-values, introducing varying degrees of shifts along the iteration (time) axis. (b)~Plots for varied $\delta \lambda $-values. (c)~Representative development of classroom spatial configuration ($L=32$, $\rho _0=0.3$) observed for different iteration numbers from $t=2$ (each column doubles the previous $t$) for TI (first row) and PI (second row) modes. The learned and unlearned states are differentiated by the color intensity, with $\lambda =0.9$ (darker) and $0.1$ (lighter) shades}{figure.4}{}}
